<title>USA: Cattle markets should work for all producers - USDA.</title>
<headline>Cattle markets should work for all producers - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Assistant U.S. Agriculture Secretary Mike Dunn said Friday the administration was committed to preventing concentration of market power in the cattle markets.</p>
<p>&quot;This administration is firmly committed to ensuring that cattle markets work for all producers,&quot; Dunn said in a statement released here.</p>
<p>&quot;I am here today to re-emphasize that commitment,&quot; the statement quoted Dunn as saying during a visit to South Dakota.</p>
<p>Dunn was to attend a forum sponsored by Democratic Sen. Tom Daschle and Rep. Tim Johnson to discuss concerns about market concentration with South Dakota producers.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
